      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The US is losing its global edge because our regulatory overreach stifles the very innovation that drives economic growth, while nations like China thrive on state-directed efficiency and minimal bureaucratic friction. By prioritizing protectionist rules over market freedom, we are artificially slowing down our industries and driving talent and capital to more agile competitors. We need to embrace deregulation to unleash the entrepreneurial spirit that once made America the world's dominant economic power.",
      "source": "target",
